 No application code, factories, system specs, or streaming specs were changed during this phase.
 
+## Factory phase (2026-11-23)
+
+Run one directory at a time with the same seed used by the configuration phases:
+
+```sh
+FPROF=1 bundle exec rspec spec/models --require test_prof --format progress --seed 1621
+FPROF=1 bundle exec rspec spec/requests --require test_prof --format progress --seed 1621
+```
+
+Before this phase, the `status` fabricator created a bookmark after every persisted status, and every persisted `user` fabricator (including role variants) created two login activities. These records were not part of the assertions in the affected examples.
+
+| Profiled group | Before: examples / factories / RSpec time | After: examples / factories / RSpec time | Time reduction |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| Models | 1,795 / 4,041 / 131.5s | 1,795 / 3,034 / 79.84s | 39.3% |
+| Requests | 1,877 / 5,760 / 120.3s | 1,877 / 3,822 / 107.19s | 10.9% |
+| Combined | 3,672 / 9,801 / 251.8s | 3,672 / 6,856 / 187.03s | 25.7% |
+
+The model profile previously contained 741 bookmarks, of which only 4 were explicit top-level uses, plus 270 login activities created entirely as factory callbacks. The request profile contained 639 bookmarks, of which only 9 were explicit, plus 1,308 callback-created login activities. After removing the callbacks, the model profile made only the 4 explicit bookmarks and the request profile made only the 9 explicit bookmarks; neither group made implicit login activities.
+
+FactoryProf's nested totals overlap. In particular, the models profile's `status` cost fell from 48.81 seconds at 0.0661 seconds per call to 16.32 seconds at 0.0221 seconds per call because the bookmark graph was no longer recorded inside every status fabrication.
+
+The final non-profiler runs used the original benchmark commands and seed:
+
+```sh
+bundle exec rspec spec/models --format progress --profile 30 --seed 1621
+bundle exec rspec spec/requests --format progress --profile 30 --seed 1621
+```
+
+- Models: 86.02 seconds RSpec execution and 89 seconds wall time, with 1,795 examples and no failures.
+- Requests: 97.59 seconds RSpec execution and 101 seconds wall time, with 1,877 examples and no failures.
+- Combined: 183.61 seconds RSpec execution and 190 seconds wall time.
+
+Compared with the pre-factory configuration-phase result (283.2 seconds RSpec execution and 291 seconds wall time), this phase reduced RSpec time by 35.2% and wall time by 34.7%. Compared with the original 434.9-second RSpec baseline and 441-second wall baseline, both groups together are 2.37x faster by RSpec time and 2.32x faster by wall time. No spec assertions, application code, system specs, or streaming specs changed in this phase.
+
+The factory rule for future work is to keep a default fabricator to the minimum valid record graph. Side-effect records should be requested explicitly in the example or made opt-in through a trait; an `after_create` callback on a common fabricator multiplies that cost across every caller.
+
 ## Follow-up opportunities
 
-- The same-seed model and request commands now total 283.2 seconds of RSpec execution versus a 434.9-second combined baseline (1.54x faster). More shared factory/setup work is still required to reach the eventual 2x target for these directories together.
-- In the factory phase, start with `account`, `status`, and `bookmark`: the models profile created each 1,194, 1,003, and 1,019 times respectively. FactoryProf nested totals overlap, so do not add them as independent runtime costs.
-- If more request gains are needed, investigate stable fixture sharing in public and link timelines, ActivityPub outboxes, and the accounts groups. Preserve per-example reload isolation and mutation rollback.
-- If more model gains are needed, investigate setup sharing in `Trends::Statuses`, `Status`, `Notification`, and `PublicFeed`; preserve per-example reload isolation and mutation rollback.
-- Keep a second seed in validation after changing shared setup; the request phase's alternate-seed run exposed no order dependency.
+- The 2x target is met. Use these 183.61-second combined and seed-specific runs as the next like-for-like baseline.
+- The largest remaining model factories are `account` (1,160 calls) and `status` (738 calls); the largest remaining request factories are `accessible_access_token` (909), `account` (704), and `status` (630). FactoryProf totals overlap, so profile a concrete change instead of summing these times.
+- Further factory work should first determine whether stable associations can be supplied from shared `let_it_be` fixtures. Avoid changing password, key, media, or callback defaults without checking behavior-specific specs.
+- Remaining high-cost setup can be revisited with RSpecDissect in `Trends::Statuses`, `Status`, `MediaAttachment`, public/link timelines, and signature verification requests. Preserve per-example reload isolation around mutable shared records.
+- Keep a second seed when introducing shared state. This factory phase changes defaults only and the same-seed model and request runs both remain isolated and green.
